# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# Enable is ignored while a stop runs (estop_disable.test's quick stop),
# then the drive enables again as usual and follows a move.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
lcnc 0 300
run 0.004
lcnc 1 0
run 0.01
fault0.stop
fault0.state
run 0.3
fault0.stop
fault0.state
lcnc 1 100
run 0.5
fault0.state
hv0.sim_vel
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 1
@expect fault0.state[1] == 0
@expect fault0.stop[2] == 0
@expect fault0.state[2] == 1
@expect fault0.state[3] == 1
@expect hv0.sim_vel[1] ~ 62.8 2%
